{"type":"message","id":"51f6ba10","parentId":"ea40ea65","timestamp":"2026-04-04T00:55:58.595Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No Chrome/Chromium available. Let me think of another approach.\n\nSince the PDF has 3 pages (based on the content: first page has 选择题 10, 12, 14, B1, B4, B5 - that's already 6 questions on the first page alone, then 填空题 starts on what seems like another page... but let me actually count the pages more carefully).\n\nActually, looking at the PDF content again, it's only a few pages. Let me try another approach - maybe I can use the macOS built-in `qlmanage` with `-t` for full page thumbnail rendering.Actually, I realize I'm overcomplicating this. \n\nThe user wants the original screenshots saved, but I can't easily render the PDF pages to images without the right tools. I could try using ImageMagick if it's available, or see if Python's pypdf2 library can help extract the pages differently. Actually, let me reconsider - the PDF might actually contain the questions as embedded images rather than text, which would explain why the file is so large.","thinkingSignature":"94fb6c69014fb0e6df2abc282b984d0f3b8196da239b14aa9d37336e9071263a"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ny8l2umhpc9i_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# 查看PDF文件大小和类型\nFILE=\"/Users/edy/.openclaw/media/inbound/è_²æ_æ_äº_å_å_å¹_çº_ç_ç_ç_ä_å_ç_ç_ä¹_20260312_ç_ç---9ac2698b-e9da-4a30-9204-b3592c66f365.pdf\"\nls -lh \"$FILE\"\n# 看看文件头\nhead -c 20 \"$FILE\" | xxd | head -3"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":15187,"output":361,"cacheRead":37857,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":53405,"cost":{"input":0.0045560999999999996,"output":0.00043319999999999996,"cacheRead":0.0022714199999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.007260719999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775264150555,"responseId":"061f949685963c2e479dd68c3572f334"}}
