ve the already-extracted text content for the question. I can use the file path directly as a reference.\n\nActually, wait - the `image` tool can analyze images, and I already have the text extracted anyway, so maybe I don't need to convert anything at all. Let me try one more approach using macOS's built-in PDF capabilities through a Python script to render pages as images directly.","thinkingSignature":"e4e18dd9dd761272c35837cd5509c59355773b95ccba0accfa7d0bcec5e1ea1f"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_cajsw961q7vu_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'PYEOF'\nimport os, sys\ntry:\n    from Quartz import PDFDocument, PDFPage, kPDFAnnotationHighlightSquare\n    print(\"Quartz PDF available!\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(f\"Quartz import error: {e}\")\n    # Try with CoreGraphics\n    try:\n        import ctypes\n        cg = ctypes.CDLL('/System/Library/Frameworks/ApplicationServices.framework/ApplicationServices')\n        print(\"CoreGraphics available\")\n    except Exception as e2:\n        print(f\"CG error: {e2}\")\nPYEOF"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":17173,"output":630,"cacheRead":37857,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55660,"cost":{"input":0.0051519,"output":0.0007559999999999999,"cacheRead":0.0022714199999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00817932}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775264181460,"responseId":"061f94b597dc9e559ccc97d91ab46ca6"}}
