{"type":"message","id":"7c0cfd00","parentId":"0a1a8760","timestamp":"2026-04-04T00:57:09.358Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No good PDF tools available. Let me just accept that I can't convert the PDF to images easily, and proceed with what I have.\n\nI'll:\n1. Save the PDF text content I already extracted to files for reference\n2. For the \"原图\" field in the bitable - I'll note that the PDF is the source document\n3. Create the bitable records with the text content I have\n\nActually, wait. The `image` tool in OpenClaw - could I pass the PDF to it? The `image` tool description says \"Analyze one or more images\" - it might accept PDFs if they can be rendered. But I think it only handles actual image formats.Let me just try: the PDF is in /tmp/openclaw/ or I can copy it there and try to analyze it with `image`.Actually, let me try a completely different approach. The image_generate tool can generate images. But what I really need is to use the existing PDF content. \n\nI'm going to stop trying to convert the PDF to images and just work with the text I've already extracted. My plan is to copy the PDF to /tmp/, create individual text files for each question, and then batch create the bitable records with the question content I've already parsed from the PDF.\n\nFor the image attachments, I'll upload the PDF itself using the feishu API with curl, since the feishu_doc_media tool with bitable_upload action should be able to handle PDF files directly as attachments. I'm going in circles trying to use the feishu_doc_media tool for PDF upload. Let me just use curl to upload the PDF directly to Feishu's drive API instead, which should give me a file_token I can use to attach to the bitable record. I'll structure the records with the question metadata and use the file_token for the attachment field. Let me just create the 9 records directly using feishu_bitable_app_table_record with batch_create, since that will be much faster than dealing with file upload complexity. I'll use the existing text I have and put the PDF URL in the notes field, plus check if there's a way to access the PDF through Feishu's file system.\n\nActually, I realize I can't attach the PDF directly to the records since there's no file_token available. Instead, I'll just include the PDF file path in the notes, then proceed with creating the records using the text content I have. For the knowledge points, I'm mapping the subject areas to their corresponding category IDs—like question 10 maps to \"力与运动\" and \"重力\" under field fldNYHZtsp. Looking at the remaining questions, I'm mapping the knowledge points for B5 which involves elastic and spring mechanics under the \"弹力\" category. For the last question about sliding friction experimental design, I need to identify which knowledge point that maps to, though it seems to be cut off. I'm going through the knowledge point mappings more carefully now—the multi-select field should use the option names rather than IDs. Looking at my list, I have friction force mapped to \"摩擦力\", force and motion to \"力与运动\", and two-force balance to \"二力平衡\", but I need to finish identifying what question 29-1 corresponds to and verify I have all the mappings complete. I'm continuing through the knowledge point mappings for the remaining questions—摩擦力 gets mapped to \"摩擦力\", and I still need to categorize question 23-1. For the diagram question 26, it should fall under 力与运动, while 29-1 about sliding friction experimental design is its own category. I'm also starting to think through difficulty levels, rating question 10 as single star since it covers the basic relationship between gravity and mass.\n\nNow I'm working through the difficulty ratings for the rest of the questions—10 is straightforward, but 12 involving Newton's First Law and circular motion is trickier, as is 14 which requires understanding of inertia and safety, and B1 on two-force equilibrium applications needs careful analysis. B4's stacked object friction problem and B5's spring and elastic force mechanics are both challenging multi-select questions. The fill-in questions vary in difficulty, with 23-1 being relatively straightforward while 26 requires both gravity and pressure concepts, and 29-1 needs experimental design skills. Now I'm setting up the batch creation of these 9 question records with their corresponding metadata. I'll structure each record with the physics subject, question content, correct answers, error analysis, knowledge points as a list, star ratings, today's date, and the PDF source file path in the notes field before pushing everything to the table.","thinkingSignature":"738d6e582dcf6c93a1a02781fc0b97ab15a2db0eccf459859c033ee634263fa9"},{"type":"text","text":"PDF 转图片工具有限，我换个思路——直接用飞书 API 上传 PDF 作为附件。先整理好题目文字内容，再批量录入。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_iuvlf5x7oann_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# 复制PDF到/tmp，尝试上传到飞书Bitable附件\nPDF_FILE=\"/Users/edy/.openclaw/media/inbound/è_²æ_æ_äº_å_å_å¹_çº_ç_ç_ç_ä_å_ç_ç_ä¹_20260312_ç_ç---9ac2698b-e9da-4a30-9204-b3592c66f365.pdf\"\ncp \"$PDF_FILE\" /tmp/xx_wrong_questions_origin.pdf\nls -lh /tmp/xx_wrong_questions_origin.pdf"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":18168,"output":1115,"cacheRead":37857,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":57140,"cost":{"input":0.005450399999999999,"output":0.001338,"cacheRead":0.0022714199999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00905982}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775264202756,"responseId":"061f94ca2920106d11f608f4cfdd66b7"}}
