{"type":"message","id":"2d139eaf","parentId":"59d2aab9","timestamp":"2026-04-04T02:00:08.062Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to be reminded at 9 PM tonight to ask Xixi for her recent biology and English exam papers. I'll create a reminder in the heartbeat system or just note it for now. Since it's about a one-time reminder for tonight, I should set up a cron-like reminder or just add it to the TODO. \n\nActually, since it's for tonight at 9 PM, and it's currently 9:59 AM, I can either:\n1. Create a one-shot cron job for 9 PM today\n2. Add it to the HEARTBEAT.md checklist for today\n3. Just note it and the user will handle it themselves\n\nGiven the user said \"提醒我今晚9点\" - they want me to remind them. The best approach is to set up a one-time cron job for today at 9 PM. Let me do that.\n\n\nI'll set up a cron job that fires once at 9 PM tonight to send a message reminding them to get the exam papers.","thinkingSignature":"70fe9a3567997ebec2256638d61efe9fca3aefd669880e3aa85aac3c94aefcd0"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_hi7k7j8qw1oh_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# 创建一次性提醒：今晚9点\n# 先获取今天9点的 datetime\npython3 -c \"\nfrom datetime import datetime\ntoday = datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%d')\nprint(f'今晚9点: {today} 21:00')\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":130,"output":283,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":63820,"totalTokens":64233,"cost":{"input":0.000039,"output":0.00033959999999999996,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.0239325,"total":0.0243111}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775267997287,"responseId":"061fa39dddb014bef3bfcf0c15bfa9f6"}}
