{"type":"message","id":"a992bbc9","parentId":"62a749fb","timestamp":"2026-04-04T02:43:37.794Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, I can do this smarter. Instead of iterating page by page, I can use the recall API with a broader search query like \"2025年12月\" and get results quickly. Or even better, the recall API already returned results mentioning 12月7日 content from other dates. Let me try \"12月6日\" specifically with recall.\n\nActually, the recall API searches semantic content, not date. Let me just wait for the list scan to complete. It should take about 50 pages * 0.2s = 10 seconds for 10 pages... but actually from the previous run, page 39 was reached, so probably about 20 more seconds.\n\n\nI'm realizing the cursor-based pagination approach is actually sound—the while loop correctly iterates through pages by checking if the oldest date on the current page has fallen below the target threshold, which means we've gone past the records we need and should stop. I'm realizing the issue with my logic—I need to check whether the target date actually falls within the current page's date range before deciding to skip it. If the newest date is on or before the target and the oldest date is on or after it, then that page contains the target date and I should keep iterating through it rather than breaking out of the loop.\n\nLet me simplify this: I'll just iterate through all pages until I find one where the oldest note is from before December 5th, which means the previous page would have December 6th notes.","thinkingSignature":"46cf88cf459481bf3671fd43bd118333cb62e9db3a41a920c81c7f87a99bc4e6"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_570f9wnlhvcj_1","name":"process","arguments":{"action":"kill","sessionId":"cool-reef"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":103338,"output":339,"cacheRead":37857,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":141534,"cost":{"input":0.0310014,"output":0.0004067999999