{"type":"message","id":"cb1d09ec","parentId":"67b178d8","timestamp":"2026-04-04T12:43:17.327Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I notice there's a bug in the python script - the `now` variable is a string from `datetime.datetime.now().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\")`, but then I'm trying to do `now[:10]` which would just give the date part \"2026-04-04\". But the string format includes spaces, so [:10] would give \"2026-04-04\". Let me fix this.\n\nAlso, I notice the line `msg = f\"📦 定时备份报告\\n\\n✅ GitHub 推送成功\\n⏰ 时间：{now}\\n📦 备份包：openclaw_backup_{now[:10]}.tar.gz\\n📁 散文件：memory/ 单独提交\"` - now[:10] would give the first 10 characters of \"2026-04-04 20:36\" which is \"2026-04-04\". That's correct. But let me check the variable name - in the f-string I use `now[:10]` which would give \"2026-04-04\". That's right.\n\n\nNow I'm realizing the core issue: I should be referencing the bash `$DATE` variable instead, which is already set to `date +%Y-%m-%d` and gives the correct date format. Let me use that in the Python section instead of trying to slice the Python datetime string.","thinkingSignature":"3f3c293e68ebbcb0a727a7332340f45ed2b05d4ce5bfdea822a59d6277a3af91"},{"type":"text","text":"顺便发现脚本里有个小 bug，Python 里 `now[:10]` 取不出日期，修正一下：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5xmtgar0340j_1","name":"edit","arguments":{"oldText":"import datetime\nnow = datetime.datetime.now().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\")\nmsg = f\"📦 定时备份报告\\n\\n✅ GitHub 推送成功\\n⏰ 时间：{now}\\n📦 备份包：openclaw_backup_{now[:10]}.tar.gz\\n📁 散文件：memory/ 单独提交\"","newText":"import datetime\nnow_str = datetime.datetime.now().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\")\ndate_str = now_str[:10]  # 取日期部分\nmsg = f\"📦 定时备份报告\\n\\n✅ GitHub 推送成功\\n⏰ 时间：{now_str}\\n📦 备份包：openclaw_backup_{date_str}.tar.gz\\n📁 memory/ 单独 commit，可查看每日变化\"","file":"/Users/edy/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/openclaw-backup.sh"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":140623,"outpu